Hey, Comrades!
We stand ready to deploy another patch in order to improve your gaming experience and this time it will be primarily focused on enhancing some of the UX/UI elements as well as text readability. The update will become available today. Please find the shortlist of changes below:

- resized the buttons on the resource management screen;
- adjusted the font used in agents’ dossiers;
- fixed an issue with the newspaper text being displayed incorrectly;
- improved the ‘attitude towards the City Committee’ and ’budget’ screens;
- applied multiple localization fixes and improvements to the Simplified Chinese version of the game.

We hope that these changes will make your gaming experience even more pleasant and thank you for your invaluable feedback!

Hey, Comrades! For the People was published on the 13th of August and today we’re ready to deploy the very first patch to improve your gaming experience. The update will be available today and here is a shortlist of the main changes:

[list]
[*] a large number of spelling, punctuation, and logical errors were fully fixed in both Simplified Chinese and German versions of the game;
[/list]
[list]
[*] when the player launches the game for the first time, it’ll now automatically open in fullscreen instead of windowed mode;
[/list]
[list]
[*] where previously your popularity among the various districts of Iron-1 was displayed in vague words (negative, indifferent, etc.) on the Citizens Attitude screen it’ll now be displayed as more precise numerical values;
[/list]
[list]
[*] the player can no longer pick up the black phone while the orange one is ringing;
[/list]
[list]
[*] the resource management system was largely rebalanced. The Wolfram Metallurgic Plant will consume more ore, other types of products will be consumed faster as well and the barter system will become even essential than before; 
[/list]
[list]
[*] putting the plant on high alert will now have a stronger negative effect on the people’s opinion towards the City Committee;
[/list]
[list]
[*] you will no longer be able to request Copper’s help on Day 10 - the player will now need to deal with the situation themselves by employing their agents;
[/list]

As always, please continue to give us your feedback about specific For the People cases that feel excessive [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1146600/discussions/0/4325098189133146829/]in this topic on Steam[/url] or in [url=https://discord.gg/h9g48vy]Discord[/url]. Thank you for your reports and patience!
